WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.025
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:09.048
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:15.983
Unit six: Feelings & Opinions. In this unit, you will talk about feelings and give opinions politely.

4
00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.042
Excited.

5
00:00:18.742 --> 00:00:21.682
Excited means very happy about something that will happen.

6
00:00:21.982 --> 00:00:23.657
I'm excited about the trip.

7
00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.114
Your turn. Say: Excited.

8
00:00:29.814 --> 00:00:30.908
Excited.

9
00:00:31.917 --> 00:00:32.953
Nervous.

10
00:00:33.653 --> 00:00:36.105
Nervous means a little afraid before something.

11
00:00:36.405 --> 00:00:38.439
I feel nervous before tests.

12
00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.745
Your turn. Say: Nervous.

13
00:00:44.445 --> 00:00:45.446
Nervous.

14
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:47.114
Proud.

15
00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:50.174
Proud means happy about something you did well.

16
00:00:50.474 --> 00:00:52.195
I'm proud of my good grade.

17
00:00:52.895 --> 00:00:55.710
Your turn. Say: Proud.

18
00:00:58.410 --> 00:00:59.144
Proud.

19
00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.105
Disappointed.

20
00:01:01.805 --> 00:01:05.546
Disappointed means sad because something was not as good as you hoped.

21
00:01:05.846 --> 00:01:07.776
He was disappointed with the score.

22
00:01:08.476 --> 00:01:10.965
Your turn. Say: Disappointed.

23
00:01:13.665 --> 00:01:14.841
Disappointed.

24
00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:16.607
Agree.

25
00:01:17.307 --> 00:01:19.411
Agree means to have the same opinion.

26
00:01:19.711 --> 00:01:20.921
I agree with you.

27
00:01:21.621 --> 00:01:24.297
Your turn. Say: Agree.

28
00:01:26.997 --> 00:01:27.847
Agree.

29
00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:29.781
Disagree.

30
00:01:30.481 --> 00:01:32.597
Disagree means to have a different opinion.

31
00:01:32.897 --> 00:01:35.326
I'm sorry, but I disagree.

32
00:01:36.026 --> 00:01:38.771
Your turn. Say: Disagree.

33
00:01:41.471 --> 00:01:42.414
Disagree.

34
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:44.220
Grateful.

35
00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.024
Grateful means wanting to say thank you.

36
00:01:47.324 --> 00:01:48.952
I'm grateful for my family.

37
00:01:49.652 --> 00:01:52.316
Your turn. Say: Grateful.

38
00:01:55.016 --> 00:01:55.832
Grateful.

39
00:01:56.817 --> 00:01:57.771
Jealous.

40
00:01:58.471 --> 00:02:01.841
Jealous means unhappy because someone has something you want.

41
00:02:02.141 --> 00:02:04.048
Don't be jealous of your friends.

42
00:02:04.748 --> 00:02:07.295
Your turn. Say: Jealous.

43
00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:10.892
Jealous.

44
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:12.815
Confused.

45
00:02:13.515 --> 00:02:15.828
Confused means not able to understand.

46
00:02:16.128 --> 00:02:17.953
I was confused by the question.

47
00:02:18.653 --> 00:02:21.433
Your turn. Say: Confused.

48
00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:25.250
Confused.

49
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.112
Relieved.

50
00:02:27.812 --> 00:02:30.403
Relieved means happy because a worry has gone.

51
00:02:30.703 --> 00:02:32.262
I was relieved when I passed.

52
00:02:32.962 --> 00:02:35.579
Your turn. Say: Relieved.

53
00:02:38.279 --> 00:02:39.095
Relieved.

54
00:02:40.083 --> 00:02:40.933
Hopeful.

55
00:02:41.633 --> 00:02:43.947
Hopeful means thinking something good will happen.

56
00:02:44.247 --> 00:02:45.886
I'm hopeful about the future.

57
00:02:46.586 --> 00:02:49.064
Your turn. Say: Hopeful.

58
00:02:51.764 --> 00:02:52.719
Hopeful.

59
00:02:53.717 --> 00:02:54.613
Curious.

60
00:02:55.313 --> 00:02:57.673
Curious means wanting to know or learn something.

61
00:02:57.973 --> 00:02:59.485
Scientists are curious.

62
00:03:00.185 --> 00:03:03.301
Your turn. Say: Curious.

63
00:03:06.001 --> 00:03:07.037
Curious.

64
00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:10.270
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:13.231
Sreypich, how do you feel before a test?

66
00:03:14.517 --> 00:03:17.120
I feel nervous, but also a bit excited.

67
00:03:18.417 --> 00:03:20.347
I think studying with friends helps.

68
00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:24.651
I agree with you. It makes me less confused.

69
00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:28.147
And how did you feel after the last test?

70
00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:32.021
Relieved and proud. I passed!

71
00:03:33.317 --> 00:03:37.255
Grammar focus: I think and I agree and I disagree.

72
00:03:37.555 --> 00:03:40.196
I think it is important. I agree with you.

73
00:03:40.496 --> 00:03:44.005
When you disagree, be polite: 'I'm sorry, but I disagree because ...'

74
00:03:45.017 --> 00:03:48.261
Now read and listen. Before and After the Test.

75
00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:51.176
Last week, we had a big English test.

76
00:03:52.483 --> 00:03:55.574
Before the test, I felt nervous and a little confused.

77
00:03:56.883 --> 00:04:00.148
My friend said, “I think we can do it,” and I agreed.

78
00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:05.284
After the test, I was relieved, and when I saw my grade, I felt proud.

79
00:04:06.583 --> 00:04:08.664
I'm grateful to my teacher for her help.

80
00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.672
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:12.972 --> 00:04:15.218
I blank with you. You are right.

82
00:04:15.518 --> 00:04:18.800
A, agree. B, disagree. C, think.

83
00:04:22.783 --> 00:04:25.050
The answer is A: agree.

84
00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:28.840
Happy because a worry has gone means blank.

85
00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:33.861
A, relieved. B, jealous. C, nervous.

86
00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.035
The answer is A: relieved.

87
00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.954
A polite way to disagree: I'm sorry, blank I disagree.

88
00:04:45.254 --> 00:04:48.397
A, but. B, and. C, so.

89
00:04:52.383 --> 00:04:54.302
The answer is A: but.

90
00:04:55.817 --> 00:04:59.711
Now it's your turn to speak. How do you feel before an important test?

91
00:05:05.011 --> 00:05:10.680
I usually feel nervous before an important test, but I think good preparation helps me feel calm.

92
00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:12.875
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:05:13.883 --> 00:05:19.415
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and i think and i agree and i disagree.

94
00:05:19.715 --> 00:05:24.271
Today's value is respectful disagreement. Disagree politely and listen to others.

95
00:05:24.571 --> 00:05:27.131
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

96
00:05:27.431 --> 00:05:30.280
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

